==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|antithesis}}, itself a borrowing from {{der|en|grc|ἀντίθεσις}}. {{surf|en|anti-|thesis}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ænˈtɪ.θə.sɪs/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-antithesis.ogg|a=US}}
{{examples|sense=rhetoric|examples=[[w:Abraham Lincoln|Abraham Lincoln]], ''[[s:Gettysburg Address|Gettysburg Address]]'' (1863)<br>The world will little note, nor long remember what we say here, but it can never forget what they did here.}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|antitheses}}

# A [[proposition]] that is the [[diametric]] [[opposite]] of some other proposition.
#: {{hyper|en|opposite|;|antipode}}
# {{lb|en|rhetoric}} A device by which two contrasting ideas are [[juxtaposed]] in [[parallel]] form; a [[figure of speech]] arranged in this manner
#* {{RQ:Langley Rhetoric|22|'''''Antithesis''''', opposing things to things,<br/>Oft from the contrast strength and beauty brings.}}
# {{lb|en|philosophy}} The second stage of a [[dialectical]] process in which the [[thesis]] is negated.

